From 51892b72a289c739a5a9084126fff457aad2743c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Thu, 2 Jul 2026 15:09:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7915: bound EEPROM access event before copying

mt7915_mcu_get_eeprom() copied a 16-byte block out of the firmware
response skb without checking that the response was long enough to hold
it. A short or malformed response could read past the end of the skb.
Reject a response shorter than the response header.

Fixes: 888208d1ccc4 ("wifi: mt76: mt7915: set correct background radar capability")
Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
 mt7915/mcu.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mt7915/mcu.c b/mt7915/mcu.c
index e19ffc70b..b963c57ec 100644
--- a/mt7915/mcu.c
+++ b/mt7915/mcu.c
@@ -2951,6 +2951,11 @@ int mt7915_mcu_get_eeprom(struct mt7915_dev *dev, u32 offset, u8 *read_buf)
 		return ret;
 
 	res = (struct mt7915_mcu_eeprom_info *)skb->data;
+	if (skb->len < sizeof(*res)) {
+		dev_kfree_skb(skb);
+		return -EINVAL;
+	}
+
 	if (!buf) {
 		u32 addr = le32_to_cpu(res->addr);
 
